            <div xml:id="d666">

                <pb facs="0790" n="1624" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1624"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/299b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-22T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 22, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1960. For Dresel [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 26. Further referring to your No. 35, Legation 3362, May 14, 6 p.m.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d666-f1"/> Five ships flying American flag aggregating over
                    30,000 tons dead weight have sailed for a French port with grain for Swiss use.
                    This includes the two vessels mentioned in Department’s 1846, May 3, 6 p.m. All
                    five ships have been sent forward under the convoy system described in
                    Department 1846. In addition to these vessels the Norwegian steamer mentioned in
                    our No. 24<anchor n="1" xml:id="d666-f2"/> is loading a cargo of foodstuffs,
                    approximately 3,700 tons to be barley and the balance lard. Two other ships
                    under the American flag have been allocated for Swiss use and question of most
                    expedient method of dispatching them is now being worked out. You are authorized
                    to make such use of the foregoing information as you see fit.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
